<title>SINGAPORE: Shell Singapore restarts 115,000-bpd crude unit.</title>
<headline>Shell Singapore restarts 115,000-bpd crude unit.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Singapore has restarted its 115,000-barrel-per-day crude distillation unit (CDU) on Monday after a one-week scheduled maintenance, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;CDU (number) four was restarted today,&quot; the spokeswoman said. The unit was shut down on July 6.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman said the startup of the crude unit will not change Shell's plan to reduce July output to 49,000 tonnes per day (tpd) from its 59,000-tpd capacity due to poor margins and high stocks of middle distillates.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3093)</p>
